                "once": true,
                "text": "\"Costing the town, they say. Carts and roofs.\" The miner spits. \"I've been costed by the yard all my life. Nobody asked me what a yard was worth either.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave them to it.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "meeting_fate",
                        "equals": "minuted"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"Written in a book downriver.\" The miner shrugs. \"My name's in a book downriver. Wages column. Doesn't keep the rain off.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave them to it.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "flag": "meeting_fate",
                        "equals": "subscribed"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"Bought in with them, I hear.\" The miner looks at your hands, which have not held a pick. \"Owners. Well. Mind how you dig.\"",
